<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32981" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτεν-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>strained</i>: hence of
			persons, <i>warmly attached, friendly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				21.22.4
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				34.2.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Socr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.31.130
			</span></i> ; <i>assiduous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
					2.277.5
				</span></i>
			 (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>): 
				Comp.
			 -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έστερος τῇ προθυμίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IGRom.</u>
					4.293a
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				ii 38
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>): 
				Sup.
			 -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εστάτη προθυμία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					2.293
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Vit.Philonid.</u>
				p.9C.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόνοια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>UPZ</u>
					110.46
				</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>extended,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				64
			</span></i>; <i>capable of extension,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐστι τὸ μεταδίδον τῶν ἑαυτοῦ καὶ
					τοῖς ἄλλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herm.
					<u>in Phdr.</u>
					p.121A.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>abundant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.94
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῶς</span> (Elean 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτενέωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>GDI</u>
					1172.12
				</span></i>
			 ; Cret. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτενίως</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5138.13
			</span></i> ; 
				Ion.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span> Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				<u>Vit.Hom.</u>
				7
			</span></i>) <i>earnestly, zealously,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαπᾶσθαι</span> Machoap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				13.579e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιεῖν τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>MM</u>
					1210a27
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συναγωνίζεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.945
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				538.17
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐχὴ ἐ. γινομένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					12.5
				</span></i>
			 : 
				Comp.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έστερον</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				13.9.1
			</span></i> : 
				Sup.
			-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έστατα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				29.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in
			Adv. also, <i>eagerly, freely, splendidly</i>
			(condemned by <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				285
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσδέξασθαί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					8.19.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				2.24
			</span></i>, etc.; of public duties, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμπρῶς καὶ ἐ. τετελεκότα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CIG</u>
					2771ii14
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Aphrodisias</span>): 
				Comp.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυτελῶς καὶ ἐκτενέστερον τῶν ἄλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Agatharch.
					<u>Fr.Hist.</u>
					6J.
				</span></i>
			—Not in early writers, corrupt in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				983
			</span></i>.</div>
